---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CTA from "../components/CTA.astro";
import { countries } from "../data/places";
import { breadcrumbs } from "../lib/schema";
---
<Base
  title="Shipping and Reship on Seizure Policy"
  description="Cold-chain packing, 24-hour dispatch, 2-5 day EU delivery, and a written reship-on-seizure policy. Carrier and timing per country."
  path="/shipping/"
  schema={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Shipping", url: "/shipping/" }])]}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Cold-chain · 24h dispatch · Written reship policy</p>
  <h1>Shipping</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Dispatch inside 24 hours of cleared payment, before the 15:00 cut-off. Sealed insulated mailer, cold pack, no
    branding, no invoice on the outside. Tracking in the same chat, same day.
  </p>

  <h2>Timing by country</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Carrier</th><th>Working days</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {countries.map((c) => (
        <tr><td>{c.name}</td><td class="mono">{c.carriers}</td><td class="mono">{c.daysMin}-{c.daysMax}</td></tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Intra-EU vs declared</h2>
  <p>
    Intra-EU clears undeclared: no customs form, no duty, no VAT bill. Switzerland, the UK, the UAE, the US and
    Canada are declared as research chemicals and carry local VAT on arrival — CHF 12 to 18 in Switzerland, HST
    plus a handling fee on a share of Canadian parcels. That is the carrier's charge, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Reship on seizure</h2>
  <p>
    If customs takes the parcel, photograph the notice and send it in the chat. We reship once, free, to the same
    address. No argument, no partial credit, no "prove it was the peptide". Claimed 14 times in four years,
    honoured every time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two conditions only: the notice has to be photographed rather than described, and the address has to be the
    one on the original order. A second seizure on the same address is reshipped at cost.
  </p>

  <h2>Packing</h2>
  <p>
    Lyophilised vials do not need dry ice. They need to not sit in a hot van, which is what the cold pack and the
    insulated mailer are for. Vials are bubble-wrapped individually so they cannot rattle, then bagged, then
    insulated. Nothing on the outside says what is inside.
  </p>

  <h2>Pickup points</h2>
  <p>
    Pickup point by default in France, Germany, the Netherlands, Poland and Sweden, because it clears faster and
    needs no signature. Home delivery on request. In the UAE, a Business Bay or Deira office address clears far
    more reliably than a villa.
  </p>

  <CTA
    src="/shipping/"
    label="Shipping page"
    heading="Ask about your country"
    body="Send the country and we will confirm carrier, days and the customs position in one message."
  />
</Base>